          "text": "45%"
        }
      ],
      "correct_answer": "B",
      "explanation": "Females in City 1 = 40% of 50,000 = 20,000. \nFemales in City 2 = 55% of 80,000 = 44,000. \nTotal Females = 20,000 + 44,000 = 64,000. \nTotal Population = 50,000 + 80,000 = 130,000. \nPercentage = (64,000 / 130,000) * 100% ≈ 49.23%. Distractors just average 40 and 55.",
