          "text": "50% ≤ x ≤ 80%"
        },
        {
          "letter": "D",
          "text": "30% ≤ x ≤ 70%"
        },
        {
          "letter": "E",
          "text": "0% ≤ x ≤ 50%"
        }
      ],
      "correct_answer": "B",
      "explanation": "The maximum overlap happens if everyone who supported A also supported B. So max(x) = min(70, 80) = 70%. \nThe minimum overlap happens if the sets are pushed apart as far as possible: P(A) + P(B) - 100% = 70% + 80% - 100% = 50%. \nThus, 50% ≤ x ≤ 70%.",
